</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.25pt;padding-bottom:-1.25pt;">single</td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.25pt;padding-bottom:-1.25pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:200.0pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.2.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Which downstream tasks does the CLiCoTEA outperform other models in terms of zero-shot performance on the IGLUE benchmark?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.25pt;padding-bottom:-1.25pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.2.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:190.0pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.2.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Your answer should be a Python list of strings, every string is the abbreviation of a downstream task type mentioned in the paper.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.25pt;padding-bottom:-1.25pt;">multiple</td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.25pt;padding-bottom:-1.25pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.2.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:200.0pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.2.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">According to this survey, what’re the three most recent decoder-only LLMs for NL2Code? How many programming languages do their training datasets each contain?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-1.25pt;padding-bottom:-1.25pt;">
